{"id":"m3-u01","level":"m3","order":1,"title":{"en":"News and media","fr":"Actualités et médias","es":"Noticias y medios","ar":"الأخبار والإعلام"},"tip":{"en":"In English, reported speech steps back in time: \"I am tired\" becomes \"She said she was tired\". Try the same with \"told\" and \"asked\".","fr":"En anglais comme en français, le discours rapporté recule dans le temps : « Je suis fatigué » devient « Elle a dit qu'elle était fatiguée ». Les titres de presse, eux, restent courts et vont à l'essentiel.","es":"En el estilo indirecto el verbo suele retroceder en el tiempo: «Estoy cansada» pasa a «Dijo que estaba cansada». Los titulares, en cambio, son breves y van al grano.","ar":"في الكلام المنقول يتغير زمن الفعل غالبا: «أنا متعبة» تصبح «قالت إنها متعبة». أما العناوين الصحفية فتكون قصيرة وتدخل في الموضوع مباشرة."},"words":46,"lessons":[{"id":"m3-u01-l1","type":"learn","order":1,"title":{"en":"the news, headline, newspaper","fr":"les actualités, gros titre, journal","es":"las noticias, titular, periódico","ar":"الأخبار، عنوان رئيسي، صحيفة"},"count":11},{"id":"m3-u01-l2","type":"learn","order":2,"title":{"en":"article, interview, broadcast","fr":"article, interview, émission","es":"artículo, entrevista, emisión","ar":"مقال، مقابلة، بث"},"count":10},{"id":"m3-u01-l3","type":"learn","order":3,"title":{"en":"rumour, fact, opinion","fr":"rumeur, fait, opinion","es":"rumor, hecho, opinión","ar":"إشاعة، حقيقة، رأي"},"count":11},{"id":"m3-u01-l4","type":"learn","order":4,"title":{"en":"to claim, to deny, to confirm","fr":"affirmer, démentir, confirmer","es":"afirmar, desmentir, confirmar","ar":"زعم، نفى، أكد"},"count":10},{"id":"m3-u01-l5","type":"learn","order":5,"title":{"en":"breaking news, live, update","fr":"dernière minute, en direct, mise à jour","es":"última hora, en directo, actualización","ar":"خبر عاجل، مباشر، تحديث"},"count":11},{"id":"m3-u01-l6","type":"learn","order":6,"title":{"en":"spokesperson, witness, account","fr":"porte-parole, témoin, témoignage","